        <!-- FAQ -->
        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">12. Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How much is a Peloton treadmill?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                On Peloton's US site on 17 October 2026, the Tread Flex was listed at about $2,195, the Tread Vision at about $3,495 and the Tread+ Vision at about $6,695, with a required $299 assembly fee on the Tread+ Vision. The All-Access Membership is extra for all three. Prices change often, so check Peloton's current listing on the day you buy.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How much is the Peloton Tread+?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                The current Tread+ model, the Tread+ Vision, was listed on Peloton's US site at about $6,695 on 17 October 2026, and a required $299 expert-assembly fee brought the total to about $6,994 before tax. The membership is separate. The original Tread+, model TR01, is no longer listed new and was recalled in 2021; check any used one for the rear guard repair.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Do you need a membership for a Peloton treadmill?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Peloton says the All-Access Membership is required to access all of its content and features on the hardware, including the class library. It also says the Just Run feature on the Tread Vision works without one, letting you set speed and incline yourself. Check the current membership price on Peloton's site and add it to the hardware cost over the years you expect to use it.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can you finance a Peloton treadmill?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Yes. On 17 October 2026 Peloton's US pages offered financing through Affirm over 12 months, at 0% APR or a higher rate depending on eligibility, and noted that a down payment may be required. The monthly figure shown covers the hardware only. Add the membership, tax and accessories to see the real monthly cost, and read the disclosure at checkout.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Does Peloton sell refurbished treadmills?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Not on 17 October 2026, as far as we could find. Peloton's US Certified Refurbished page listed refurbished bikes only. Used Peloton treadmills do appear on local marketplaces; check the model number for recall status, ask for a factory reset, and remember the membership still applies, along with a one-time activation fee Peloton charges for used equipment.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is a used Peloton Tread+ safe to buy?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Only once you have confirmed its recall status. The original Tread+, model TR01, was recalled in 2021 because people, children, pets and objects could be pulled under the rear. A free breakaway rear guard repair was approved in 2023. Check the model sticker on the front of the deck, ask whether the guard has been fitted, and confirm with Peloton before you pay.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div class="mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes When Pricing a Peloton Treadmill</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Most Peloton budgeting mistakes come from looking at one number when there are at least three.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Leaving out the membership</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The listed price is the hardware only. The classes and most features need the All-Access Membership, which continues every month for as long as you want them. Multiply the current monthly price by the months you expect to use the treadmill and add it to the hardware before comparing with any other machine.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Forgetting the assembly fee on the Tread+</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The Tread+ Vision requires expert assembly, and on 17 October 2026 that added $299 at checkout. The cheaper models offer free delivery with self-assembly, but the boxes are heavy and need at least two people. Compare delivered, assembled prices, not list prices, and check delivery terms if you live outside the continental US.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Treating the home trial as risk-free</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Peloton's 30-day home trial is for first-time buyers in the 48 contiguous states, requires payment up front and has return fees. It is a useful safety net, not a free rental. Decide whether you like the classes first, through the Peloton App on a phone or tablet, before relying on a trial return.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying a used Tread+ without checking the recall</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">A TR01 Tread+ was recalled for a rear pull-under hazard, and a free rear guard repair was later approved. Read the model sticker at the front of the deck, ask whether the guard was fitted, and confirm with Peloton. A cheap used Tread+ without the repair is not a bargain in a home with children or pets.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

